---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import socialCards from "../config/socialCards.json";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Tyler Crosse works on machine learning and AI safety, from research experiments to production systems."
  image={socialCards.about.image}
  imageAlt={socialCards.about.alt}
>
  <div class="headshot slide-in-block">
    <Image
      src="/img/headshot.jpeg"
      alt="Tyler Crosse"
      width={300}
      height={300}
    />
  </div>

  <section class="intro slide-in-block">
    <h1>Hi, I'm Tyler</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      I work on machine learning and <strong>AI safety</strong>, from research
      experiments to production systems. I recently completed projects with
      Redwood Research on attack selection for AI control and with SPAR on
      scalable oversight. I also have more than seven years of production
      software engineering experience, most recently as a senior engineer and
      team lead. I completed Georgia Tech's MSCS in May 2026, with a focus on
      machine learning and computing systems.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="journey slide-in-block">
    <h2>My path</h2>
    <p>
      My undergraduate degree is in <strong>Biomedical Engineering</strong>. I
      ended up in software, where I worked on consumer products, enterprise
      search, data pipelines, developer tooling, and distributed services. That
      work taught me how to turn prototypes into systems people can rely on and
      how to make tradeoffs when correctness, performance, and delivery all
      matter.
    </p>
    <p>
      Seeing the early results from
      <a
        href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaFold"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">AlphaFold</a
      > in 2018 pushed me to study machine learning more seriously. As language
      models became more capable and agentic, I became interested in a narrower
      set of questions: what safety evaluations actually measure, how models
      behave under pressure, and how to build experiments that make those
      failures visible. I returned to school to add deeper ML and systems
      foundations to my production engineering background.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="research slide-in-block">
    <h2>Recent research</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>AI control with Redwood Research:</strong> I studied how an
        attacking agent's decision to start or abandon an attack changes the
        apparent safety of control protocols. Selective start/stop policies
        reduced measured safety by roughly 20–28 points at a 1% audit budget
        across BashArena and LinuxArena. The project began through MARS 4.0 and
        continued as a collaboration with Redwood.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Agent evaluation and scalable oversight with SPAR:</strong> In
        Fall 2025, I built evaluation infrastructure for measuring goal drift
        in long-horizon coding agents. In Spring 2026, I worked on human-AI
        oversight and built the FastAPI backend for a participant study run
        through Prolific.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      I also completed ARENA 7.0 in London. For the capstone, I used activation
      patching, steering vectors, and path patching to study how moral
      fine-tuning changes attention pathways in Gemma-2-2b.
    </p>

    <h3>Selected publications</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.06529"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          ><em
            >Attack Selection in Agentic AI Control Evaluations Meaningfully
            Decreases Safety</em
          ></a
        >, co-first author. Accepted to the ICML 2026 AI4GOOD and AI-WILD
        workshops and as a FAGEN poster; under review at NeurIPS 2026.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.04161"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          ><em
            >When Offline Selectors Cannot Beat the Best Single Model</em
          ></a
        >, first author. Accepted to the ICML 2026 DEMO Workshop.
      </li>
      <li>
        Three co-authored papers from SPAR, including work on inherited and
        asymmetric goal drift in coding agents and inference effects in medical
        allocation.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      My full publication list is on <a
        href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=RfFEQLMAAAAJ&hl=en&oi=ao"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Scholar</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="experience slide-in-block">
    <h2>Industry experience</h2>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>Knowable</h3>
          <p class="company">
            Senior Software Engineer &amp; Team Lead
            <span class="period">| Jun 2019 – Jun 2024</span>
          </p>

          <p class="description">
            Directed the technical roadmap for a five-engineer team building a
            legal knowledge platform. I took RAG-style LLM and OpenSearch
            systems from data-science prototypes to production over several
            million contracts, built event-driven services on AWS, and cut the
            average CI pipeline from roughly 55 minutes to 15. I also maintained
            a React component library used across three product teams.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>Rosetta Stone</h3>
          <p class="company">
            Software Engineer
            <span class="period">| Aug 2017 – Jun 2019</span>
          </p>

          <p class="description">
            Rebuilt a React and Node marketing platform with page loads about
            2.25 times faster. I also built an internal A/B testing system used
            by roughly 20 non-engineering stakeholders to run hundreds of
            experiments and maintained backend services for a platform serving
            millions of learners.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="education slide-in-block">
    <h2>Education</h2>
    <div class="timeline">
      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>Georgia Institute of Technology</h3>
          <p class="company">
            MS Computer Science <span class="period">| May 2026</span>
          </p>

          <p class="description">
            Focused on machine learning and computing systems. Coursework
            included deep learning, reinforcement learning, GPU hardware and
            software, high-performance computer architecture, Advanced
            Operating Systems, and Graduate Algorithms. Projects included
            FlashAttention and KV-cache CUDA kernels, GPU simulators, static
            branch-divergence analysis, and reproducible ML evaluation
            pipelines.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline-item">
        <div class="timeline-marker"></div>
        <div class="timeline-content">
          <h3>Virginia Commonwealth University</h3>
          <p class="company">
            BS Biomedical Engineering <span class="period">| Dec 2023</span>
          </p>

          <p class="description">
            Studied engineering, physiology, and the design of systems for
            medical and biological problems.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="interests slide-in-block">
    <h2>What I'm interested in</h2>
    <div class="interests-grid">
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>🧩 Mechanistic Interpretability</h3>
        <p>
          Sparse autoencoders, circuits, and tools to open up black boxes so we
          can understand and steer models.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>🎯 AI Safety & Alignment</h3>
        <p>
          Building systems that are steerable, reliable, and beneficial by
          design.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>🛡️ Robustness & Evaluation</h3>
        <p>
          Empirical evaluation under distribution shift; honesty/helpfulness
          metrics; reproducibility and measurement.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>🔧 Systems for ML</h3>
        <p>
          Operating systems, distributed systems, and tooling that make ML
          research reliable, scalable, and repeatable.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>⚡ High-Performance Computing</h3>
        <p>
          GPU programming, parallelism, computer architecture, and the memory
          systems underneath modern models.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>📚 Learning in Public</h3>
        <p>
          Sharing the journey—methods, failures, and breakthroughs—so others can
          learn alongside me.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>⚖️ Economics</h3>
        <p>Understanding the economic forces that shape our world.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="interest-card">
        <h3>🧬 Computational Biology</h3>
        <p>
          Understanding the biological mechanisms that underlie disease and
          development.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="about-this-site slide-in-block">
    <h2>About This Digital Garden</h2>
    <p>
      This is where I keep technical write-ups, research notes, course
      retrospectives, and project logs. Some pieces are finished articles;
      others are notes that I update as my understanding changes.
    </p>
    <p>
      I try to include the method, mistakes, and intermediate reasoning instead
      of only the final result. If you notice an error or want to discuss
      something, <a href="mailto:hello@tylercrosse.com">send me a note</a>.
    </p>

    <p>
      Built with <a
        href="https://astro.build/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro</a
      >. Check out the <a
        href="https://github.com/tylercrosse/personal-site"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">source code</a
      >.
    </p>

    <details class="inspiration-details">
      <summary>Sites that inspired this one</summary>
      <ul class="inspiration-list">
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://distill.pub/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            <strong>Distill.pub</strong>
          </a> - Interactive machine learning research papers
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://maggieappleton.com/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            <strong>Maggie Appleton</strong>
          </a> - The digital garden philosophy and beautiful visual thinking
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.arlenmccluskey.com/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            <strong>Arlen McCluskey</strong>
          </a> - Clean technical writing and site structure
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://eugeneyan.com/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            <strong>Eugene Yan</strong>
          </a> - Thoughtful ML content and career insights
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://www.swyx.io/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            <strong>Swyx</strong>
          </a> - Learning in public and developer advocacy
        </li>
        <li>
          <a
            href="https://lowyx.com/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            <strong>Yxlow</strong>
          </a> - Minimalist design and thoughtful curation
        </li>
      </ul>
    </details>
  </section>

  <style>
    section {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 2rem auto;
      padding: 0 1rem;
    }

    .headshot {
      margin: 2rem auto;
      max-width: 300px;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .headshot img {
      border: 8px solid #fff;
    }

    .intro {
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 3rem;
    }

    .intro h1 {
      font-size: 2.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      color: var(--sol-base01);
    }

    .lead {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--sol-base0);
      max-width: 600px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .journey {
      margin-bottom: 3rem;
    }

    .journey p {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }

    .research p,
    .research li {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .research ul {
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }

    .timeline {
      position: relative;
      /* margin: 2rem 0; */
    }
    .timeline-item {
      position: relative;
      margin-bottom: 2rem;
      /* padding-left: 60px; */
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }

    .timeline-marker {
      position: absolute;
      left: 11px;
      top: 8px;
      width: 18px;
      height: 18px;
      border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--sol-base2);
      border: 3px solid var(--sol-base3);
    }

    .timeline-content h3 {
      color: var(--sol-base01);
      font-size: 1.4rem;
    }

    .company {
      color: var(--sol-blue);
      font-weight: 600;
      margin: 0 0 0.25rem 0;
    }

    .description {
      color: var(--sol-base0);
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin: 0;
    }

    .interests-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem;
      margin: 2rem 0;
    }

    .interest-card h3 {
      margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
      color: var(--sol-base01);
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }

    .interest-card p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--sol-base0);
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    /* .about-this-site {
        background: var(--sol-base3);
        border-radius: 12px;
        padding: 2rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--sol-base2);
      } */

    .about-this-site p {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }

    .inspiration-details {
      margin-top: 2rem;
    }

    .inspiration-details summary {
      cursor: pointer;
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--sol-base01);
      padding: 0.5rem 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sol-base2);
    }

    .inspiration-details summary:hover {
      color: var(--sol-blue);
    }
    .inspiration-list li {
      margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
      padding-left: 1rem;
      position: relative;
    }

    .inspiration-list a {
      color: var(--sol-blue);
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .inspiration-list a:hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .slide-in-block {
      opacity: 0;
      filter: blur(10px);
      transform: scale(0.95);
      will-change: transform, opacity, filter;
      animation: slideInBlock 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.43, 0.195, 0.02, 1) forwards;
    }

    .slide-in-block:nth-child(1) {
      animation-delay: 0s;
    }
    .slide-in-block:nth-child(2) {
      animation-delay: 0.1s;
    }
    .slide-in-block:nth-child(3) {
      animation-delay: 0.2s;
    }
    .slide-in-block:nth-child(4) {
      animation-delay: 0.3s;
    }
    .slide-in-block:nth-child(5) {
      animation-delay: 0.4s;
    }
    .slide-in-block:nth-child(6) {
      animation-delay: 0.5s;
    }

    @keyframes slideInBlock {
      to {
        opacity: 1;
        filter: blur(0px);
        transform: scale(1);
      }
    }

    /* Dark theme adjustments */
    @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
      .headshot img {
        /* border-color: var(--sol-base02); */
      }

      .interest-card {
        background: var(--sol-base02);
        border-color: var(--sol-base01);
      }

      .about-this-site {
        background: var(--sol-base02);
        border-color: var(--sol-base01);
      }

      .timeline::before {
        background: var(--sol-base01);
      }

      .timeline-marker {
        background: var(--sol-base01);
        border-color: var(--sol-base02);
      }
    }

    /* Mobile responsive */
    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .intro h1 {
        font-size: 2rem;
      }

      .lead {
        font-size: 1.1rem;
      }

      .interests-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .timeline-item {
        padding-left: 50px;
      }

      .timeline::before {
        left: 15px;
      }

      .timeline-marker {
        left: 6px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
